10 REM CIRCLES - THE NEAL-PITTEWAY MIDPOINT INTEGRATOR
20 REM X = X - E / 2 * Y : Y = Y + E * X : X = X - E / 2 * Y, WITH E = 1 / 16
30 REM ONE TURN IS 2 * PI / E STEPS: S RUNS TO 104 OR EACH RING IS AN OPEN ARC
40 REM APPLESOFT HAS FLOATING POINT, SO A RADIUS IS PIXELS AND NOT SCALED
50 REM HI-RES PIXELS ARE SQUARE ON THIS SCREEN, SO NO ASPECT TERM EITHER
60 HGR
70 FOR K = 1 TO 3
80 HCOLOR= K * 2 - 1
90 X = K * 22
100 Y = 0
110 HPLOT 140 + X,80
120 FOR S = 1 TO 104
130 X = X - Y / 32
140 Y = Y + X / 16
150 X = X - Y / 32
160 REM HPLOT TO JOINS THE LAST POINT TO THIS ONE, SO THE RING IS A LINE
170 REM AND NOT A DOTTED TRACK
180 HPLOT TO 140 + X,80 + Y
190 NEXT S
200 NEXT K
210 END
